{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"JLSEC-2026-1428","published":"2026-11-23T20:01:46.351Z","modified":"2026-11-23T20:15:04.588891432Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-53796","EUVD-2026-58035"],"details":"rsync before 3.5.0 contains a time-of-check to time-of-use (TOCTOU) race condition vulnerability in the non-daemon receiver's destination directory handling that allows an attacker who can manipulate destination path parent components to redirect file writes to unintended locations. Attackers can substitute a symlink for a component of the destination path between the path resolution and chdir() call, causing the receiver's working directory to be established outside the intended destination tree so that subsequent relative-path file writes land in unintended filesystem locations.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"rsync_jll","ecosystem":"Julia","purl":"pkg:julia/rsync_jll?uuid=191d6b87-264a-55f5-a0e2-c8fbce9a1ce0"},"ranges":[{"type":"SEMVER","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"3.5.0+0"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/JuliaLang/SecurityAdvisories.jl/tree/generated/osv/2026/JLSEC-2026-1428.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/RsyncProject/rsync/releases/tag/v3.5.0"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/RsyncProject/rsync/security/advisories/GHSA-w75h-ccff-w53m"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/rsync-toctou-race-condition-via-destination-directory-handling"}],"database_specific":{"license":"CC-BY-4.0","sources":[{"affected":{"samba:rsync":["< 3.5.0"]},"database_specific":{"status":"Analyzed"},"html_url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-53796","id":"CVE-2026-53796","imported":"2026-11-21T02:56:04.995Z","modified":"2026-11-06T16:00:11.540Z","published":"2026-08-13T15:19:51.553Z","url":"https://services.nvd.nist.gov/rest/json/cves/2.0?cveId=CVE-2026-53796"},{"html_url":"https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/EUVD-2026-58035","id":"EUVD-2026-58035","imported":"2026-11-21T02:56:06.499Z","modifie